                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2042832c-933d-4f10-8144-5b136bfb9b38",
                        "source_entry_id": "a960cc1c-99e2-354f-95e7-db350e8efbc7",
                        "source_sense_id": "ef1d37d7-3c7d-31a6-a1fd-fb13acab631a",
                        "target_lang_word": "shagreen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shagreen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e2ec98d-83ae-3d9e-a348-e661f8ac9622",
                                        "entry_id": "2ae9d273-dbe4-35f0-8174-91eb804880b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An untanned leather, often dyed green; originally made from horse skin, today mostly made from the skin of a shark or ray."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79d5ef2b-1332-4043-b174-149c324200fd",
                                                "sense_id": "3e2ec98d-83ae-3d9e-a348-e661f8ac9622",
                                                "text": "The following day the treasures of the mysterious tower came pouring in: pictures, statues, gems, shells, china, stuffed beasts and birds, tables, vases, petrifactions, arms, mandarins, &c. &c.; and among them the shagreen skin, with the injunction, \"Sell it for any thing—nothing—give it away; only, get rid of it.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f091c9b-b677-4060-85ac-0d7466ad58b3",
                                                "sense_id": "3e2ec98d-83ae-3d9e-a348-e661f8ac9622",
                                                "text": "On the old lecturn or reading-stand which he used for his heavier tomes, The Testaments of Carnamagos, in its covers of shagreen with hasps of human bone, lay open at the very page which had frightened him so unreasonably with its eldritch intimations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56b99a07-3c12-3878-a088-f28109c0be93",
                                        "entry_id": "2ae9d273-dbe4-35f0-8174-91eb804880b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rough or spiny surface of an insect's cuticle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7801cd88-2d05-4ca7-b4f9-6938bd556fee",
                                                "sense_id": "56b99a07-3c12-3878-a088-f28109c0be93",
                                                "text": "If the shagreen dots be carefully observed they will be found to possess an annular arrangement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58a0e3d1-11c7-42fb-9d12-4caf43e505a6",
                                                "sense_id": "56b99a07-3c12-3878-a088-f28109c0be93",
                                                "text": "The shagreen of the abdominal tergites generally consists of small spinules, singly or in caudally convex arcs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shagreen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "223e80a3-415f-33d4-a509-80d4d3f7d2af",
                                        "entry_id": "c671890c-f6ea-3ac3-a2f9-dc2b5eaf98ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give a texture resembling shagreen leather."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "56e61a7a-40cd-4080-b159-82bb4ca779c8",
                        "source_entry_id": "a960cc1c-99e2-354f-95e7-db350e8efbc7",
                        "source_sense_id": "ef1d37d7-3c7d-31a6-a1fd-fb13acab631a",
                        "target_lang_word": "chagriné",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chagriné",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "298d87d1-0cfb-34ee-b254-09aaed798fc1",
                                        "entry_id": "50d934df-2939-3613-9562-bfe1e437a4a8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a l’apparence du chagrin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69fd1356-6e0f-4e8e-a595-4e311b0cf365",
                                                "sense_id": "298d87d1-0cfb-34ee-b254-09aaed798fc1",
                                                "text": "Agnès et Bruno ressentirent un étonnement chagriné à ne pas avoir vu venir cette mort que Pompidou portait sur lui, corps alourdi, visage bouffi, ils avaient voulu croire aux grippes à répétition et aux crises hémorroïdaires qui expliquaient sa démarche embarrassée."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "304b0481-e48d-3b5d-adf4-425cfc4a281f",
                                        "entry_id": "50d934df-2939-3613-9562-bfe1e437a4a8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a l’apparence du cuir grenu."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6f4f71f-1e53-453e-a50b-d443ccd673b0",
                                                "sense_id": "304b0481-e48d-3b5d-adf4-425cfc4a281f",
                                                "text": "Le fruit est une pyxide, à une loge renfermant un grand nombre de graines, à surface chagrinée, rattachées à un trophosperme central."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6712d41-b6ec-4de3-accf-5e60fe750920",
                                                "sense_id": "304b0481-e48d-3b5d-adf4-425cfc4a281f",
                                                "text": "On affirmait dans la famille : « Le fard abîme le teint. » Mais nous nous disions souvent ma sœur et moi en voyant la peau chagrinée de nos tantes que leur prudence payait mal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5aabcde-7fc9-4dbc-a555-5ef68ae2d592",
                                                "sense_id": "304b0481-e48d-3b5d-adf4-425cfc4a281f",
                                                "text": "Le plus beau galuchat provient de la pastenague, raie géante dont la queue comporte un aiguillon armé d’une scie des deux côtés. Il est chagriné, c’est-à-dire grenu naturellement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "chagriné",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17ee1255-b14b-39b6-828d-f1ec5f3b48df",
                                        "entry_id": "9ca9ef52-f503-3efb-8352-a5e5fe4b9aec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Participe passé masculin singulier du verbe chagriner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
